  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 225 AM EDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nA broad ~1030 mb sfc high anchored over Ontario, the northern Great \nLakes and Quebec will continue to provide a feed of cool \neasterly flow through the remainder of the week. Clouds and \npockets of lighter rain showers will also remain in the forecast\nthrough Wednesday as deeper moisture lingers in the lowest 10 \nkft, and an upper level vort over Iowa meanders east into the \nlower Great Lakes. Best chances for measurable light rain \n(20-30%) will be this afternoon into Wednesday along and east \nof the Interstate 69 corridor where slightly better moisture \nprofiles will linger.\n\nThe second half of the week into the upcoming weekend then features \nmore in the way of sunshine and gradual air mass modification as the \nupper vort exits off to the east, eventually phasing into a larger \nlow pressure system just off the Mid Atlantic coast. This blocking \npattern will favor ridging/subsidence over the local area.",
